WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.723
Governance starts with knowing what is stored, what

00:00:03.723 --> 00:00:07.095
rules apply, and who is responsible for those

00:00:07.095 --> 00:00:07.517
decisions.

00:00:07.917 --> 00:00:11.672
Review the schedule’s scope and status. Read the

00:00:11.672 --> 00:00:15.427
stated authority and confirm that it applies before

00:00:15.427 --> 00:00:17.304
enabling any retention behavior.

00:00:17.704 --> 00:00:21.064
A hold changes how the affected records should

00:00:21.064 --> 00:00:24.424
be handled. Verify the behavior in a disposable

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:27.784
environment rather than assuming a label is enough.

00:00:28.184 --> 00:00:31.357
Open the inventory and inspect what it reports.

00:00:31.357 --> 00:00:34.529
Read its gaps as well as its totals.

00:00:34.529 --> 00:00:37.702
The inventory is an input to review, not

00:00:37.702 --> 00:00:39.288
a substitute for one.

00:00:39.688 --> 00:00:43.084
Export the inventory and compare it with the

00:00:43.084 --> 00:00:46.480
screen. Keep the date and deployment context so

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.452
another reviewer knows what the document describes.

00:00:49.852 --> 00:00:53.815
Decide the scope, document the authority, and verify

00:00:53.815 --> 00:00:57.778
the behavior. These controls support your process; they

00:00:57.778 --> 00:01:01.741
do not confer approval or compliance by themselves.
